Pri-Hum-Fem-Law
atheist, genocideless, wishless, artiwishless, polyselfless,
polypileless

I've been attempting to ascend 6-conduct character for quite some
time. I
first tried with orcish barbarian, but in order to compete in
Junethack I
switched to priest in AceHack, hoping it will be easier. I didn't
manage to
win in time (and even if I did, someone else did 9 conduct anyway). I
thought atheist priest should be quite easy, but it still took many
games to
succeed. Today I finally managed to ascend 6-conduct game in vanilla
NetHack.

1) Started with the most useless spellbooks possible: create monster
and cure
blindness.

2) First done Sokoban (amulet of reflection).

3) Minetown very disappointing, no magic lamp, no bag/sack.

4) Some very very close calls while diving deeper. I found early ring
of
polymorph control that I used for protection from polytraps. Funny
enough, I
ran into none until the Quest.

5) Found spellbook of identify quite early, that made things much
easier.

6) I made green dragon scale mail from a throne room dragon to get rid
of my
+3 chain mail that hindered my spellcasting. All my fail rates went to
0%
immediately.

7) With no way of getting past Medusa I decided to embark on the
Quest,
hoping to find some important items there. At this point, I still had
no
bag/sack, no means of levitation and, most importantly, no MR, making
Nalzok
a threat. Also, while I have seen number of black and gray unicorns, I
was
yet to see single white one, which means my luck is still low. I
prepared
for the Quest enchanting my silver saber to +4.

8) On the upper filler level I ran into a polytrap, which robbed me of
two
XL's with associdated HP/Pw loss.

9) On the locate level I found the item I needed most -- plain sack.
Until
this moment I had no portable container. I also upped my silver saber
to +5
and my unicorn horn to +2. Since I got quite some wraith corpses, I
reached
XL 20 (from the XL 12 I got to at above level due to a polytrap). Good
thing, since I could cast magic missile at 0% and do some damage. This
is
quite important, since I never upgraded my primary weapon to an
artifact.

10) On the lower filler level I accidentaly fell through a trapdoor
dug by a
wraith with wand of digging. Since I had no MR, I was quite afraid of
Nalzok. But he remained sleeping all the way to upstairs. There I
burnt
Elbereth and for a while tried to wake him up, finally succeeding. He
took I
think four blows from my +5 silver saber before succumbing. Other
important
loot from the Quest was a blessed scroll of genocide. As genocideless,
blessed is useless, but now I could either curse it or write another
cursed
scroll for reverse genocide. Another important find somewhere on the
quest
was spellbook of haste self -- I never found speed boots, so having
hasting
was quite useful.

11) I decided that before proceeding to Medusa, I'll consolidate my
stashes to
the level above Medusa and make a batch of holy/unholy water. During
the
consolidation I found ring of teleport control.

12) After consolidating to dlvl 23 stash I made use of a blessed
scroll of
remove curse to make unholy water through that obnoxiously tedious
process.
I cursed my blessed scroll of genocide, revgenocided gray dragons and
got
three sets of scales and after enchanting I had +4 GDSM. Magic
resistance
at long last, and also freed ring slot (polycontrol no longer
necessary).

13) Once again I got arch-lich (and master lich as a bonus) right on
arrival
to the Castle (by digging, so I was far from upstairs). I killed the
master
lich with magic missile and the arch-lich conveniently summoned two
cockatrices.

14) Food storeroom at the Castle was empty save for one giant ant,
that had
nothing in its inventory.... where did that food go? Anyway, there was
nothing useful in the inventory but long sword (to make Excalibur,
which I
didn't). I still had no means of levitation.

15) Cleared VoTD but no way of getting back, so I entered Gehennom,

16) Found bag of holding on the second level of Gehennom.

17) Lost all scrolls save blessed charging and most potions in Juiblex
swamp. Note to self: Don't dig pits next to water. I also noticed,
that my
ring of TC is missing. Either I misplaced it, or it got disintegrated
by
some chest trap.

18) Found another BoH at Orcus, which had ring of teleport control
inside!
There was another =oTC at Orcus. Got wand of death from Orcus' statue.
Chickatrice petrified me, so I lost my intrinsic speed and had no /oSM
at
hand. Then I returned to my dlvl 23 stash by levelporting.

19) I packed all the stash into BoH and went beck (yes, the original
=oTC was
in the stash, so now I had 3 rings of TC).

20) The Medusa titan somehow turned hostile and started summoning. Or
was it
hostile to start with?

21) Because I forgot "haste self" spell and wasn't even fast, I did i
quick
return to Home 3 level to fetch some spellbooks I stashed there.

22) VS level on dlvl 45 -- I think it must be the shallowest I had? I
usually
have to delve to dlvl 50 or so.

23) I returned to my VoTD stash and prepared for the run: a) used last
chunk
of MM to fireproof water walking boots in preparation for the Plane of
Fire;
b) used two found scrolls of enchant weapon to up my unicorn horn to
+7, I
had given up on making Excalibur after few attempts that only dried
fountains; c) alchemized full healing (got to HP 273 with 10 FH
potions
left); d) I still had no permanent means of levitation, so I prepared
four
blessed potions of levitation to cross the Plane of Air and Water.

24) I have found uncursed scroll of genocide on the second level of
the
Wizard's Tower, so I returned to stash, where I cursed it and  reverse
genocided white unicorns and finally improved my luck! BTW, the game
dump
shows that there really were no white unicorns generated in my game!

25) Returned to Rodney's residence and petrified him with chickatrice.
After
invocation I levelported to the Sanctum, where I ended conveniently in
the
open space and quickly retrieved the Amulet from the high priest.

26) The journey to the surface was unexpectedly easy, the mysterious
force
triggered only about four times (compare that with 18 times for my
neutral
archeologist). I used scroll of earth to cross Castle trapdoors.

27) After doing the Plane of Earth (my only wand of death had just
enough
charges to deal with the Wizard) I put on ring of conflict and quaffed
blessed potion of levitation and wrote down the turn count. To my
complete
amazement, I managed to do the three planes above Earth on single
potion
(that is within 250 turns). I was very afraid of the Plane of Water in
particular, but it turned out to be complete non-issue.

28) Astral was easy as I took the right turn and found my altar on the
first
try, only having to kill Death once.

